            ],
            "sectionHeading": "Our charges",
            "quote": "For researching, recommending and arranging these investments, we charge an initial advice fee of 3% of the amount invested as per the terms stated in our Client Agreement. In monetary terms this is 9,838.36 with current transfer values, this figure may fluctuate depending on transfer values. This will be paid directly by the pension scheme on transfer."
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Ongoing advice charges of 1% per annum. Based on current values and expected contributions, minus the initial fee, this would be equal to circa \u00A33,181.08 for the first year. This will vary in line with your fund value. This fee will be paid via the Aviva Platform pension scheme.",
          "topic": "OngoingAdviceCharges",
          "isClientSpecific": true,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Recommended",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "H_SolutionDesign",
            "pageNumbers": [
              22
            ],
            "sectionHeading": "Future contact and ongoing services",
            "quote": "The costs for this service are 1% per annum. Based on current values \u0026 expected contributions, minus the initial fee, this would be equal to circa \u00A33,181.08 for the first year."
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "You should note that whilst the transactions are pending, there could be movements within the stock-market; that is to say that the stock-market could rise or fall in value. If the market rises in value between the date of realising your existing funds and the purchase of your new funds, you could be financially disadvantaged insofar as the cost of buying your new fund could be greater. Conversely, if there is a fall in the market between the date of realising your existing funds and the purchase of your new funds, you could be financially advantaged insofar as the cost of buying your new funds could be lower.",
          "topic": "OutOfMarketRisk",
          "isClientSpecific": true,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Actual",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "H_SolutionDesign",
            "pageNumbers": [
              10
            ],
            "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Should you require access to these funds in the future it will usually take 10-15 working days for administration, disinvestment and banking processes to complete. You are comfortable with the concept as you have liquid cash should you require instance access funds.",
          "topic": "WithdrawalTimescale",
          "isClientSpecific": true,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Reported",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "H_SolutionDesign",
            "pageNumbers": [
              10
            ],
            "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "There is no guarantee the return on the new investment will be greater than that of your existing arrangement for these funds.",
          "topic": "NoGuaranteeOfReturn",
          "isClientSpecific": false,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Actual",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "H_SolutionDesign",
            "pageNumbers": [
              10
            ],
            "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "All other risks associated with this investment are detailed in the product literature provided to you. You should read this document carefully.",
          "topic": "ProductDocumentation",
          "isClientSpecific": false,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Actual",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "H_SolutionDesign",
            "pageNumbers": [
              10
            ],
            "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "You have a legal right to change your mind and cancel your plan. Once your plan is set up you will be sent a cancellation notice. You have 30 days to review and consider your options. You should check the provider literature to confirm the date this period commences as well as any charges that may apply following cancellation. If your investment falls in value before your cancellation notice is received, an amount equal to the fall in value will be deducted. However, please be aware the cancellation notice includes a provision that any previous provider is not obliged to take the plan back.",
          "topic": "CancellationRights",
          "isClientSpecific": false,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Actual",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "H_SolutionDesign",
            "pageNumbers": [
              21
            ],
            "sectionHeading": "Cancellation notice"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "I recommend that you complete the nomination of beneficiaries\u0027 form that will be provided to you after the transfer process is begun. This will allow you nominate who you wish to benefit from your funds on passing. It will also allow you to designate an amount of your funds to several people.",
          "topic": "BeneficiariesNomination",
          "isClientSpecific": true,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [
            "OBJ1",
            "OBJ8"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Recommended",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "H_SolutionDesign",
            "pageNumbers": [
              21
            ],
            "sectionHeading": "Nominations and death benefits"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "All payments will be subject to Aviva\u0027s discretion. Where your nominees withdraw from the proceeds it will be tax free should you die before age 75. Where your death occurs on or after age 75 those payments will be subject to the nominee\u0027s marginal rate of tax.",
          "topic": "DeathBenefitsTaxation",
          "isClientSpecific": false,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [],
          "provenance": {
